From 2a73d622a96d0795aa01c8958006275c96686290 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurag Reddy Gunreddy <gunreddyg@google.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:25:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] feat(cluster): add MinRefreshInterval and MaxSlotWait

Add two ClusterOption fields that bound the topology refreshes of a
cluster client and let requests wait for a shard to get a primary back.
Both are off by default. With the zero values the client behaves as
before: a request for a slot without a node refreshes once and fails
with ErrNoSlot.

MinRefreshInterval rate-limits topology refreshes. When the last refresh
finished less than MinRefreshInterval ago, a request that finds no node
for its slot re-reads the current slot map instead of refreshing again,
and a lazy refresh (MOVED, connection errors, ShardsRefreshInterval)
waits until the interval has passed. The lazy refresh checks this when
its random delay is over rather than when it is scheduled, so it also
waits for a refresh that finished in between.

MaxSlotWait bounds how long a request waits for its slot to have a node,
for example while a shard has no online primary during a failover. A
waiting request re-reads the slot map each time a refresh finishes, and
starts a refresh in the background when none is in flight, at most once
per MinRefreshInterval or 10ms, whichever is longer. The waiting
requests share these refreshes and do not poll: call.next returns the
refresh in flight, or the one that starts next, and they wait for it to
finish. The request is sent as soon as its slot has a node. It fails
with ctx.Err() when its context ends, with ErrClosing as soon as the
client is closed, and after MaxSlotWait with the error of the last
refresh it waited for, or ErrNoSlot. NewClient rejects negative values
(ErrInvalidMinRefreshInterval, ErrInvalidMaxSlotWait).

Signed-off-by: Anurag Reddy Gunreddy <gunreddyg@google.com>
