diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index d3f76e6..b500d64 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -516,6 +516,20 @@ Note that scaling the number of replicas on an existing shard (e.g. via ElastiCa
 neither moves slots nor closes existing connections, so without `ShardsRefreshInterval`
 the client never discovers the new replicas and continues reading the old shard.
 
+While a shard has no primary, during a failover for example, a request for one of its slots refreshes the
+topology and fails with `ErrNoSlot` at once, so a busy client can refresh the topology hundreds of times a
+second until the new primary appears. To bound the refreshes and let requests wait for the new primary instead:
+
+```golang
+client, err := valkey.NewClient(valkey.ClientOption{
+    InitAddress: []string{"127.0.0.1:7001", "127.0.0.1:7002", "127.0.0.1:7003"},
+    ClusterOption: valkey.ClusterOption{
+        MinRefreshInterval: 250 * time.Millisecond, // refresh the topology at most once every 250ms
+        MaxSlotWait:        5 * time.Second,        // wait up to 5s for a slot without a node instead of failing with ErrNoSlot
+    },
+})
+```
+
