From 5e183b8d257c18ecf4e375b27ffdf82ddeb6eac6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurag Reddy Gunreddy <gunreddyg@google.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 07:28:30 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/7] perf(cluster): don't refresh the topology on ASK

An ASK reply means that the slot is being migrated and is still owned by
the node that replied, so the slot map is right and a topology refresh
has nothing to learn. The MOVED replies that follow the migration
refresh it. While a migration runs, every command for a key that has
already moved gets ASK, and each of them scheduled a lazy refresh. Now
only MOVED, CLUSTERDOWN, TRYAGAIN, LOADING and connection errors do.

Signed-off-by: Anurag Reddy Gunreddy <gunreddyg@google.com>
