From da6f61ecd8b7c5e48bca15c6ace01a0e154368ce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anurag Reddy Gunreddy <gunreddyg@google.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 09:55:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] fix(cluster): pace MOVED redirect loops

Nodes that disagree on the owner of a slot redirect a command to each other.
The client followed them at network speed until the command's context ended,
and forever without a deadline. A redirect back to the node the command was
first sent to also replaced that node's connection each time, because the
"MOVED to the same address" reconnect compared the target with the first
node instead of the node that sent the redirect.

The client now follows two MOVED redirects of a command directly, so a slot
that moved twice costs no wait. From the third one, it waits for the
topology refresh that MOVED schedules and routes the command by the
refreshed slot map, one round per refresh, until the nodes agree, the
context ends or the client is closed. DoMulti and DoMultiCache do the same
from their third round of redirects. The reconnect compares the target with
the node that sent the redirect, so it happens when that node names its own
address, as intended for endpoints that resolve to a new node, and not in a
loop.

The slot reconnect test now expects the reconnection to :0, which redirects
the command to its own address, and the connections of the refresh that the
third MOVED waits for.

